8:T659,{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"How does the wheel-to-ski conversion work on the Gravity Cart Sport?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The GC-SPORT-01 chassis mounts its terrain interface at the same certified attachment points year-round. Swapping to winter use means releasing the wheel assembly and engaging the Ski Assembly Kit (GC-SKI-200) — a tool-free binding, no separate frame."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What terrain and grade is the ski conversion rated for?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The GC-SKI-200 ski assembly is 780mm in length and rated to a 25% descent grade on packed snow, fitted to the GC-SPORT-01 chassis."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What braking hardware does the Gravity Cart Sport use?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The Shimano Dual Brake Kit (GC-BRK-180) is a hydraulic dual-disc set with 180mm front and rear rotors, tested against the ECE R100 braking standard."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is the load rating of the certified chassis?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The GC-SPORT-01 chassis is rated to 120kg, with certified wheel and ski assemblies included, engineered for pavement, gravel and packed snow."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is the Gravity Cart Sport CE and ISO compliant?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. The Gravity Cart Sport is independently tested and documented against ECE 2006/42/EG, ISO EN 12100 and ISO EN 4210 — the same category of machinery and safety directives that govern the automotive and machinery industries."}}]}0:{"P":null,"b":"yNmA_oew2rdrZXTCE1_6K","p":"","c":["",""],"i":false,"f":[[["",{"children":["__PAGE__",{}]},"$undefined","$undefined",true],["",["$","$1","c",{"children":[[["$","link","0",{"rel":"stylesheet","href":"/_next/static/css/7685a5a8d879318d.css","precedence":"next","crossOrigin":"$undefined","nonce":"$undefined"}]],["$","html",null,{"lang":"en","className":"__